{"id": "ecd36219-5843-483d-ae26-2dc14f3c65d1", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:01:04.606950", "source": "user", "parent_id": "28429983-f690-41e4-8847-8a35c65509c3", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Before we design anything, please do a light reconnaissance pass only — no experiment design yet.\\n\\n1) Inspect the working environment at /workspace (and any attached notes) and report what is actually present: any InfLLM code, config files, retrieved-memory / unit-representation implementations (e.g. similarity metric, top-k retrieval, memory unit size / block size, context-memory window), benchmark harnesses, and any task lists or dataset manifests that are referenced (e.g. LongBench-style, needle-in-a-haystack, retrieval/length-generalization evals). If nothing relevant is present, say so plainly rather than assuming.\\n\\n2) Summarize, strictly from what you find (or from clearly labeled general knowledge if the repo is empty), how InfLLM is structured: which components would count as \\\"dynamic context memory lookup\\\" (retrieval key/value source, similarity computation, top-k selection, whether the query attends over retrieved blocks vs. recent contiguous context) and which knobs would count as \\\"unit representations\\\" (block/unit granularity, pooled vs. token-level unit embeddings, whether units come from the LM's own hidden states vs. a separate encoder, positional treatment across units).\\n\\n3) Propose 2-3 candidate framings for how this question could be answered experimentally — e.g. an ablation-ladder design, a matched-budget representation swap, or a diagnostic/transfer analysis — with a one-line rationale for each and what each would and would not let us conclude. Do not commit to a design yet.\\n\\n4) List the consequential assumptions and unknowns you are making: which model scale/variants are in scope, what task families we treat as \\\"long-context tasks\\\", what budget (GPU-hours, number of runs) we can realistically assume given no GPU is enabled here, and whether this must remain a pure design document with feasibility argued rather than executed.\\n\\nKeep it to inspection, structure summary, candidate framings, and open questions.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How critical are dynamic context memory lookup and the choice of unit representations to InfLLM’s performance across long-context tasks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
